; Regression test for issue #3243: how payees matching the xact payee
; pattern rank against the other candidates.
;
; A Payee tag that matches the pattern counts like a matching payee, and
; an exact match still outranks every pattern match, even when regex
; metacharacters keep the payee from matching itself as a pattern:
; "SQ *COFFEE" matches "SQ COFFEE" but not "SQ *COFFEE".  Below the
; threshold of 30, recency alone ranks the matches, as it did when
; draft_t::insert fell back to the most recent payee matching the pattern.

2026-06-20 * Union Hardware
    Expenses:Household:Home:Hardware       14.99 USD
    Liabilities:CC:American Express

2026-06-25 * Lowes: flapper-seal and light-bulbs
    Expenses:Household:Home:Lowes          31.87 USD
    Liabilities:CC:American Express

2026-06-26 * Costco
    ; Payee: Nothing Bundt
    Expenses:Household:Food:Takeout         5.99 USD
    Liabilities:CC:American Express

2026-06-27 * SQ *COFFEE
    Expenses:Household:Food:Coffee          4.50 USD
    Liabilities:CC:American Express

2026-06-28 * SQ COFFEE
    Expenses:Household:Food:Cafe            6.25 USD
    Liabilities:CC:American Express

test --now 2026/06/30 xact bundt
2026/06/30 Costco
    ; Payee: Nothing Bundt
    Expenses:Household:Food:Takeout         5.99 USD
    Liabilities:CC:American Express
end test

test --now 2026/06/30 xact "SQ *COFFEE"
2026/06/30 SQ *COFFEE
    Expenses:Household:Food:Coffee          4.50 USD
    Liabilities:CC:American Express
end test

; "Union Hardware" resembles "Un" more than the Payee tag "Nothing Bundt"
; does, but neither reaches 30, so the more recent Costco transaction wins.
test --now 2026/06/30 xact Un
2026/06/30 Costco
    ; Payee: Nothing Bundt
    Expenses:Household:Food:Takeout         5.99 USD
    Liabilities:CC:American Express
end test
